From: pmOS Mi8Lite <macosmojave2@gmail.com>
Subject: [PATCH] arm64: dts: qcom: sdm660-xiaomi-platina: enable WCN3990 Bluetooth

Enable the WCN3990 Bluetooth (hci_qca serdev on the BLSP2 UART1 4-wire
port). It is the same combo die as the already-working WiFi; the four
VDD rails are shared with &wifi and ref-counted by the regulator core.
This mirrors the known-working sdm660-xiaomi-lavender BT config, and
adds the serial1 alias lavender uses for the BT UART.

Split out of the old 0022-platina-bt-vibrator so BT and the vibrator can
be validated (and, if needed, bisected) independently on the device.

Signed-off-by: pmOS Mi8Lite <macosmojave2@gmail.com>
--- a/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm660-xiaomi-platina.dts	2026-07-15 15:35:10.645379298 -0500
+++ b/arch/arm64/boot/dts/qcom/sdm660-xiaomi-platina.dts	2026-07-15 15:35:10.670546665 -0500
@@ -26,6 +26,7 @@
 
 	aliases {
 		serial0 = &blsp1_uart2;
+		serial1 = &blsp2_uart1; /* Bluetooth UART */
 	};
 
 	chosen {
@@ -1159,3 +1160,22 @@
 &sound {
 	pinctrl-0 = <&cdc_pdm_default>, <&cdc_dmic_default>, <&sec_mi2s_default>;
 };
+
+/*
+ * Bluetooth: WCN3990 combo chip (shares the die with the WiFi) on the
+ * BLSP2 UART1 4-wire port via hci_qca. The four VDD rails are the same
+ * ones the WiFi (&wifi) votes for the shared chip; the regulator core
+ * ref-counts them. Mirrors the known-working sdm660-xiaomi-lavender BT.
+ */
+&blsp2_uart1 {
+	status = "okay";
+
+	bluetooth {
+		compatible = "qcom,wcn3990-bt";
+		vddxo-supply = <&vreg_l9a_1p8>;
+		vddrf-supply = <&vreg_l6a_1p3>;
+		vddch0-supply = <&vreg_l19a_3p3>;
+		vddio-supply = <&vreg_l13a_1p8>;
+		max-speed = <3200000>;
+	};
+};
